SWEET WLAN patch 0154 (lane W, plan oneshot-2 review prerequisites before any store level after the CA7 release): review 0150 G1 (= review 0150-1 F3) and review 0147 N3,
plus the small items 0150 G2 (citations). Levels <= 7 store exactly what they stored before; the new checks only refuse.
G1 (glue, sweet_wlan.c sw3_wr): an independent gate for the CA7 release: a CA7-wrapper IOCTL value without CPUHALT (SICF_CPUHALT 0x20, DHD include/siutils.h:306 at 865527e) is refused
    unless the stage 3 level is 7 and the one reset-vector store at backplane address 0 happened in this boot (rv_done, patch 0132). The first such store latches h->released; after it
    every BAR2 store is refused by the glue, independent of the header's tuple table. A later level that needs chip-RAM stores after the release (host_cap, rings) must add its own,
    explicitly gated exception in sw3_wr. The latch is set just before the store; the CA7 restore (RESET_CTL := 1) and cfg 0x80/0x84 stay allowed.
N3 (header + glue): swl_fwids[] rows carry the board they were observed on (bluejay: 1764018 B crc 0x1153ccff, run wd3; oriole: 1764091 B crc 0x92567396, run wlan-oriole-l4);
    swl_fw_known(len, crc, board) needs all three. The board is swl_board_id() of the root ADT property model-number (tools/mkadt.py build() writes the board name; observed "oriole",
    7 bytes with the NUL, in A.adt of run o3-w5-l7); anything else is board 0 and pins nothing (levels 4-7 then stop before the first store, as with an unknown image).
G2: citation texts: W16 comment (DHD MAX_READ_TIMEOUT 2 s, dhd_pcie.c:594-598; bwfm poll if_bwfm_pci.c:869-875, range :880-881 at 9d8cbe8); rings_info_ptr include/bcmpcie.h:384.
    (The 0150 patch header still says "868-874 ... DHD 5 s"; the reviewed 0150 file is left as it is and this note corrects it.)
New log line: "SWEET WLAN: stage 3 board N (model-number, 1 bluejay 2 oriole, 0 unknown)".
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c (board binding, swl_board_id, review 0150 G3/G6 cases); tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py (chain + 0154, new mutants, glue sweep of the release gate and latch).

